[175.249711, "o", "\u001b[4mGIT-PUSH\u001b[24m(1)                           Git Manual                          \u001b[4mGIT-PUSH\u001b[24m(1)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mNAME\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       git-push - Update remote refs along with associated objects\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mSYNOPSIS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[4mgit\u001b[24m \u001b[4mpush\u001b[24m [--all | --branches | --mirror | --tags] [--follow-tags] [--atomic] [-\u001b[m \b\u001b[4m\u001b[24m\u001b[4m\u001b[24mn | --dry-run] [--receive-pack=<git-receive-pack>]\u001b[m\r\n                  [--repo=<repository>] [-f | --force] [-d | --delete] [--prune] [-q |\u001b[m \b --quiet] [-v | --verbose]\u001b[m\r\n                  [-u | --set-upstream] [-o <string> | --push-option=<string>]\u001b[m\r\n                  [--[no-]signed|--signed=(true|false|if-asked)]\u001b[m\r\n                  [--force-with-lease[=<refname>[:<expect>]] [--force-if-includes]]\u001b[m\r\n                  [--no-verify] [<repository> [<refspec>...]]\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       Updates remote refs using local refs, while sending objects necessary to\u001b[m\r\n       complete the given refs.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       You can make interesting things happen to a repository every time you push\u001b[m\r\n       into it, by setting up \u001b[4mhooks\u001b[24m there. See documentation for \u001b[1mgit-receive-pack\u001b[22m(1).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       When the command line does not specify where to push with the \u001b[1m<repository>\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       argument, \u001b[1mbranch.*.remote \u001b[22mconfiguration for the current branch is consulted to\u001b[m\r\n       determine where to push. If the configuration is missing, it defaults to\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[4morigin\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       When the command line does not specify what to push with \u001b[1m<refspec>...\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       arguments or \u001b[1m--all\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m--mirror\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m--tags \u001b[22moptions, the command finds the default\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1m<refspec> \u001b[22mby consulting \u001b[1mremote.*.push \u001b[22mconfiguration, and if it is not found,\u001b[m\r\n       honors \u001b[1mpush.default \u001b[22mconfiguration to decide what to push (See \u001b[1mgit-config\u001b[22m(1)\u001b[m\r\n       for the meaning of \u001b[1mpush.default\u001b[22m).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       When neither the command-line nor the configuration specifies what to push,\u001b[m\r\n       the default behavior is used, which corresponds to the \u001b[1msimple \u001b[22mvalue for\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1mpush.default\u001b[22m: the current branch is pushed to the corresponding upstream\u001b[m\r\n       branch, but as a safety measure, the push is aborted if the upstream branch\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page git-push(1) line 1 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[176.727969, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       does not have the same name as the local one.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page git-push(1) line 2 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[177.075096, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page git-push(1) line 3 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
